module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.CoherentPullbackUnderEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesToposPullback
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Five more local types of modules are intrinsic

Stacks 03DM asserts that each of the eight local conditions of Stacks 03DL on a sheaf of modules
on a ringed site is intrinsic in the sense of Section 03DG: it holds for a module if and only if
it holds for the pullback of that module along an equivalence of ringed topoi.  This file proves
that for the clauses

1. locally free,
2. finite locally free,
3. locally generated by sections,
6. quasi-coherent, and
8. coherent,

for an arbitrary equivalence of ringed topoi between ringed topoi on Stacks sites.  The clauses
(4) locally generated by `r` sections, (5) of finite type and (7) of finite presentation are
proved at the same generality in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence`, and the shape of the
argument is taken from there.  With the clause (8) below, all eight clauses of Stacks 03DL are
now proved intrinsic.

Each statement is an `iff` whose forward implication is, for the first four clauses,
Stacks 03DO, which for them holds for an *arbitrary* morphism of ringed topoi and is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules` and its companions in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesToposPullback`.  The reverse
implication applies the same lemma to the inverse morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.inverse` and transports the conclusion back along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesInverseObjIso`, the identification of the round
trip with the identity, using the invariance of the clause under an isomorphism of sheaves of
modules.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DM for
  the clause 03DL (1).**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`:
  **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (2).**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`:
  **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (3).**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DM
  for the clause 03DL (6).**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isCoherentOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`: **Stacks 03DM for
  the clause 03DL (8).**

## Implementation notes

The two ringed topoi live in the universes of a Stacks site, `RingedTopos.{w, w, w}`, which is
the generality Stacks 03CR — and hence the four 03DO lemmas the forward implications are — is
available at; at those universes every sheafification hypothesis the argument uses is an
instance, so none is assumed.  This is narrower than
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence`, whose three clauses
need no site replacement and so allow the two ringed topoi independent universes.

The inverse morphism is written `inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f` rather than `inverse f`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.inverse` is stated for ringed topoi in six independent
universes, and leaving them to be solved against the four-universe-equal statement of the 03DO
lemma leaves unsolved universe metavariables inside the elaboration of the pullback, which
exhausts the heartbeat budget.  For the same reason the universe arguments of the 03DO lemmas
and of the invariance lemma for the clause (3) are given explicitly.

The clause 03DL (8), coherence, does not share that forward implication: Stacks 03DO omits it,
and necessarily so — see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesToposPullback` for the counterexample.
Its forward implication is instead
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isCoherentOnSite_pullbackModules`, which runs on the
*one-sided* factorization of an equivalence of ringed topoi, the addendum to Stacks 03CR, whose
middle arrow is a change of coefficient rings on a single replacement site rather than a
morphism of sites.  Its reverse implication is taken along the inverse equivalence exactly as
the four above.  The clause for the restriction of modules along a special cocontinuous functor
of sites, which is one side of that factorization, is
`Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isCoherentOnSite_iff`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom

universe w

variable {X Y : RingedTopos.{w, w, w}} (f : RingedToposHom X Y)
  [f.toToposHom.pushforward.IsEquivalence] [IsIso f.fSharp]
  (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Y.O))

/-- **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (1): local freeness is intrinsic.**  A sheaf of modules on
the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is locally free if and only if its pullback is.

The forward implication is Stacks 03DO.  The reverse one applies Stacks 03DO to the inverse
equivalence and carries the conclusion back along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesInverseObjIso`. -/
@[stacks 03DM "locally free"]
theorem isLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_pullbackModules :
    F.IsLocallyFreeOnSite ↔ (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsLocallyFreeOnSite :=
  ⟨isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules f F, fun hP ↦
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
      (pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules.{w} (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f) _ hP)⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (2): finite local freeness is intrinsic.**  A sheaf of
modules on the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is finite locally free if and only if
its pullback is; the rank on each member of the covering is unchanged in both directions. -/
@[stacks 03DM "finite locally free"]
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_pullbackModules :
    F.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite ↔
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite :=
  ⟨isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules f F, fun hP ↦
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_of_iso
      (pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_pullbackModules.{w} (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f) _ hP)⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (3): local generation by sections is intrinsic.**  A sheaf
of modules on the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is locally generated by sections if
and only if its pullback is; the index type of the generating family is unchanged in both
directions. -/
@[stacks 03DM "locally generated by sections"]
theorem isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_pullbackModules :
    F.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite ↔
      (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite :=
  ⟨isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules f F, fun hP ↦
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Intrinsic.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_iso.{w, w, w}
      (pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_pullbackModules.{w}
        (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f) _ hP)⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (6): quasi-coherence is intrinsic.**  A sheaf of modules on
the target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is quasi-coherent if and only if its pullback
is. -/
@[stacks 03DM "quasi-coherent"]
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff_pullbackModules :
    F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite ↔ (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
  ⟨isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules f F, fun hP ↦
    SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso
      (pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isQuasicoherentOnSite_pullbackModules.{w} (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f) _ hP)⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (8): coherence is intrinsic.**  A sheaf of modules on the
target of an equivalence of ringed topoi is coherent if and only if its pullback is.

The forward implication is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isCoherentOnSite_pullbackModules`,
which is *not* an instance of Stacks 03DO — that tag omits coherence, and could not state it.
The reverse one applies the forward implication to the inverse equivalence and carries the
conclusion back along `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModulesInverseObjIso`. -/
@[stacks 03DM "coherent"]
theorem isCoherentOnSite_iff_pullbackModules :
    F.IsCoherentOnSite ↔ (f.toModulesHom.pullbackModules.obj F).IsCoherentOnSite := by
  have : (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f).toToposHom.pushforward.IsEquivalence :=
    inferInstanceAs f.toToposHom.inverseImage.IsEquivalence
  have : IsIso (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f).fSharp :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsIso (inv f.fSharpInverseImage))
  exact ⟨isCoherentOnSite_pullbackModules f F, fun hP ↦
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_of_iso (pullbackModulesInverseObjIso f F)
      (isCoherentOnSite_pullbackModules.{w} (inverse (X := X) (Y := Y) f) _ hP)⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom

end
